{"title":"Career roadmap · Climate Data Analyst","role":"Climate Data Analyst","summary":"A Climate Data Analyst works with environmental, meteorological, oceanographic, satellite, and socioeconomic datasets to identify climate trends, assess climate risks, build indicators, and support adaptation, mitigation, policy, research, and sustainability decisions.","facts":{},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Climate Data Analyst works with environmental, meteorological, oceanographic, satellite, and socioeconomic datasets to identify climate trends, assess climate risks, build indicators, and support adaptation, mitigation, policy, research, and sustainability decisions."},{"type":"p","text":"A B.Sc in Climate Science, Climate Change Studies, Environmental Science, Atmospheric Science, Earth Science, Geography, Physics, Mathematics, Statistics, or a closely related discipline can provide a foundation for this career."},{"type":"p","text":"The most employable profile combines:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Climate Science","Statistics","Python/R","Geospatial Data","Remote Sensing","Data Visualisation"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Typical employers include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Climate research organisations"},{"text":"Environmental consultancies"},{"text":"Sustainability teams"},{"text":"Government agencies"},{"text":"Research institutes"},{"text":"Development organisations"},{"text":"Energy companies"},{"text":"Agriculture and water organisations"},{"text":"Climate-risk and ESG analytics firms"},{"text":"Universities and think tanks"}]}]},{"heading":"Career horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Stage","Typical role","Main focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"B.Sc Student"},{"text":"Climate + mathematics + statistics"}],[{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Data/Research Intern"},{"text":"Environmental datasets and analysis"}],[{"text":"Year 3"},{